Z||000014||JetroGT||09-30-2000||11:17 PM||||The other pictures were supposed to be of the engine and the car with doors, hood, and deck lid open. Oh well. <BR>I orignally bought the car last winter from an insurance company. It had a junk title so I got it cheap. The front end was pushed in and bent to the left. Everything needed to be replaced.  I drove up to Fiero Daves place and got a white fender from an 84. I already had a hood, front cover, and the right fender from an 86 GT. The body shop cut the whole front end off up to the first part of the front compartment. Then welded on the front end from my 86 GT parts car. Since then I've replaced a ton of stuff.<BR>Head liner<BR>clutch peddel rubber<BR>custom Fiero floor mats<BR>new manaul shift knob<BR>front berings, roaters, pads<BR>all engine mounts<BR>tranny mounts + rear tranny support<BR>added console tray, dash mat<BR>and I still have about twice that more to do!<BR>It's a good thing I like working on my car  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000015||Cliff Pennock||10-01-2000||03:49 AM||||JetroGT, the filename contains spaces which is a no-no... The forum's software can't handle that. If you download the latest PIP patch (only a 40K download or so), PIP will automagically replace those spaces for underscores when you upload.||||reg||1
